sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch02-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In polymorphic genera such as Rubus, Rosa and Hieracium, the inordinate variation concerns structures that are of no service or disservice to the species and so have not been seized on and made definite by natural selection.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polymorphic genera vary in traits of no use, unfixed by selection";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter II, “Variation under Nature”; section “Individual Differences”. Scope: polymorphic genera of plants, insects and brachiopods"
}
